    async def create(
        self,
        *,
        stock_type: str,
        quantity: int,
        price: float,
        reference: Optional[str] = None,
        portfolio_id: Optional[str] = None,
        lwin18: Optional[str] = None,
        warehouse_code: Optional[str] = None,
        condition_status: Optional[str] = None,
        condition_text: Optional[str] = None,
        duty_paid: Optional[bool] = None,
        cost: Optional[float] = None,
        inbond_address_id: Optional[int] = None,
        extra_headers: Optional[Mapping[str, str]] = None,
        extra_query: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,
        extra_body: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,
        timeout: Union[float, httpx.Timeout, None] = None,
        max_retries: Optional[int] = None,
    ) -> Write[OfferResult]:
        """Create an offer.

        List a line of your portfolio stored with Cru, wine you hold outside Cru, or your own
        stock as a supplier, for sale at a price per unit you choose.

        **Wine stored with Cru or held outside it, or a supplier’s own stock.** stock_type cru
        puts units of a line of your portfolio stored with Cru on sale. stock_type external
        lists wine in your own storage, for accounts Cru has set up to sell it. stock_type
        supplier adds an offer of your own stock, for a supplier whose offer feed Cru imports.
        To sell into a bid now, POST /market/bids/{code}/sell.

        **A line stored with Cru.** Its units go on sale at your price, and you receive it less
        Cru’s commission: the listed line’s pricing gives commission_percent, commission and
        net_proceeds. Listing moves them to a listed line with a portfolio_id of its own, not
        the one you sent, so take the answer’s for PATCH and DELETE /offers/{code}. A line
        already listed is refused: change its price or quantity with PATCH /offers/{code}
        instead. Removing the offer later only takes it off sale.

        **Your next offer feed import replaces a supplier offer.** An offer listed with
        stock_type supplier joins your offers on Cru only until your next offer feed import to
        Cru, which replaces it, as it replaces all your offers: your feed stays the source of
        truth. To keep selling the wine, put it in your feed too.

        **A supplier offer.** It is sold from your own warehouse, so it takes no warehouse_code,
        and it must be priced in your offer feed’s currency: on a Cru site that quotes in
        another, it is refused with TRADE_REFUSED, and the message names the currency. Its line
        comes back with stock_type supplier, and your price as both pricing.listing_price and
        pricing.net_proceeds. You can change it afterwards with PATCH /offers/{code}, like any
        of your supplier offers.

        **Removing wine held outside Cru takes it out of your portfolio.** Listing wine held
        outside Cru creates its units in your Cru portfolio, in bond. Removing the offer later
        deletes them again.

        Scope: offers:write.

        A partner credential's write runs at once and returns the result in .result; a connected
        app's is staged, with the code to confirm in .confirmation.

        Args:
            reference: Your idempotency key: letters and digits, then . _ : or - allowed.
                Required on a partner credential’s write and kept for good, so a retry with it
                can never act twice. Ignored for connected apps.
            stock_type: What you are listing: cru, a line of your portfolio stored with Cru;
                external, wine you hold outside Cru; or supplier, your own stock as a supplier
                whose offer feed Cru imports. The fields below that say which of them they are
                for are refused for the others, with VALIDATION_UNKNOWN_PARAMETER. Anything
                else, bpo included, is refused with VALIDATION_INVALID_VALUE: BPO stock cannot
                be listed through the API.
            portfolio_id: The line to list, from GET /portfolio: one with stock_type cru that is
                not listed yet (is_listed false). Its units go on sale as a listed line with a
                portfolio_id of its own, which the answer gives. Only with stock_type cru.
            lwin18: The wine. Cru must trade it. Only with stock_type external or supplier.
            quantity: Units to list. For cru, at most the line’s quantity.
            price: Price per unit in the market’s currency, to at most 2 decimal places. For cru
                and external, the asking price, what the buyer pays: the line’s
                pricing.listing_price. For supplier, what you receive: buyers pay Cru’s price,
                and the line gives yours as both pricing.listing_price and pricing.net_proceeds.
            warehouse_code: The Cru warehouse it is sold through: one GET /warehouses marks
                sells_your_inbond_wine for you. The line gives it back as
                warehouse.deliverable_warehouse_code. Only with stock_type external.
            condition_status: verified (Verified), client_reserves (Client Reserve) or apd (As
                per description). For external, it defaults to, and cannot exceed, the level Cru
                set for your account. For supplier, it defaults to verified, or to apd when
                duty_paid is true, which takes nothing else. Only with stock_type external or
                supplier.
            condition_text: What buyers are told about the condition. Required for apd, and
                refused for verified; client_reserves may have it. Duty-paid stock says “Duty
                Paid in the UK” unless you give it. Only with stock_type supplier.
            duty_paid: true when the duty has been paid, which makes the offer apd. Defaults to
                false, in bond. Only with stock_type supplier.
            cost: What you paid per unit, for your records. Only with stock_type external.
            inbond_address_id: The inbond warehouse the wine is in now, from GET
                /warehouses/inbond. Leave it out if you are not sure where the wine is: Cru
                records it as not sure, as the website’s “Not Sure” option does. Only with
                stock_type external.
            extra_headers: Headers to add to, or replace, the SDK's own, for this call only.
            extra_query: Query parameters this version does not know yet, sent as given.
            extra_body: Body fields this version does not know yet, sent as given.
            timeout: Seconds, or an httpx.Timeout, for this call only. None keeps the client's.
            max_retries: Retries after the first attempt, for this call only. None keeps the
                client's.
        """
        return await self._client._call(
            _CREATE_OFFER,
            body={
                'reference': reference,
                'stock_type': stock_type,
                'portfolio_id': portfolio_id,
                'lwin18': lwin18,
                'quantity': quantity,
                'price': price,
                'warehouse_code': warehouse_code,
                'condition_status': condition_status,
                'condition_text': condition_text,
                'duty_paid': duty_paid,
                'cost': cost,
                'inbond_address_id': inbond_address_id,
            },
            extra_headers=extra_headers,
            extra_query=extra_query,
            extra_body=extra_body,
            timeout=timeout,
            max_retries=max_retries,
        )

    async def get(
        self,
        code: str,
        *,
        extra_headers: Optional[Mapping[str, str]] = None,
        extra_query: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,
        timeout: Union[float, httpx.Timeout, None] = None,
        max_retries: Optional[int] = None,
    ) -> PortfolioWine:
        """Retrieve one of your offers.

        One listed line of your portfolio, by its portfolio_id: its wine as GET /offers gives
        it, with that line alone.

        **One item of GET /offers.** data.offer is what GET /offers gives as one item of
        data.offers: the same wine and fields, with only the line whose portfolio_id you gave
        under portfolio, and total_quantity its units. A listing’s code gives the wine with all
        the listing’s lines.

        **offers:read shows what the wine cost.** GET /offers and GET /offers/{code} need
        offers:read, not portfolio:read, yet their lines carry everything GET /portfolio’s do,
        pricing.cost included: a credential that can read your listings sees what the listed
        wine cost you.

        Scope: offers:read.

        Args:
            code: A listed line’s portfolio_id, from GET /offers, GET /portfolio or the offer a
                write answered with, to read just that line’s units. A listing’s LISTING- code
                also works, for the whole listing. URL-encode it as a single path segment.
            extra_headers: Headers to add to, or replace, the SDK's own, for this call only.
            extra_query: Query parameters this version does not know yet, sent as given.
            timeout: Seconds, or an httpx.Timeout, for this call only. None keeps the client's.
            max_retries: Retries after the first attempt, for this call only. None keeps the
                client's.
        """
        return await self._client._call(
            _GET_OFFER,
            {'code': code},
            extra_headers=extra_headers,
            extra_query=extra_query,
            timeout=timeout,
            max_retries=max_retries,
        )

    async def update(
        self,
        code: str,
        *,
        reference: Optional[str] = None,
        price: Optional[float] = None,
        quantity: Optional[int] = None,
        extra_headers: Optional[Mapping[str, str]] = None,
        extra_query: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,
        extra_body: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,
        timeout: Union[float, httpx.Timeout, None] = None,
        max_retries: Optional[int] = None,
    ) -> Write[OfferResult]:
        """Change an offer.

        Change the asking price or quantity of one listed line of your portfolio, or of a whole
        listing. A repriced line comes back with a new portfolio_id.

        **What a change does depends on where the wine is.** Held outside Cru (external): a
        lower quantity deletes units, a higher one creates them. Stored with Cru: units come off
        or go on sale, up to what you hold in that warehouse. Supplier offers take a lasting
        override. BPO stock cannot be changed.

        **Change one line, or a whole listing.** Given a listed line’s portfolio_id, only that
        line’s units change: the preview’s before and after quantities are the line’s, and its
        code the listing’s. A lower quantity takes units off that line alone. Repriced, the line
        gets a new portfolio_id, which the offer in the answer carries. Given a listing’s code,
        every line of the listing changes.

        Scope: offers:write.

        A partner credential's write runs at once and returns the result in .result; a connected
        app's is staged, with the code to confirm in .confirmation.

        Args:
            code: A listed line’s portfolio_id, from GET /offers, GET /portfolio or the offer a
                write answered with, to act on just that line’s units. A listing’s LISTING- code
                also works, for the whole listing. URL-encode it as a single path segment.
            reference: Your idempotency key: letters and digits, then . _ : or - allowed.
                Required on a partner credential’s write and kept for good, so a retry with it
                can never act twice. Ignored for connected apps.
            price: New price per unit, in the market’s currency, as GET /offers and GET
                /portfolio quote it: pricing.listing_price. A supplier offer’s is converted into
                your offer feed’s currency.
            quantity: New quantity. Send price, quantity or both.
            extra_headers: Headers to add to, or replace, the SDK's own, for this call only.
            extra_query: Query parameters this version does not know yet, sent as given.
            extra_body: Body fields this version does not know yet, sent as given.
            timeout: Seconds, or an httpx.Timeout, for this call only. None keeps the client's.
            max_retries: Retries after the first attempt, for this call only. None keeps the
                client's.
        """
        return await self._client._call(
            _UPDATE_OFFER,
            {'code': code},
            body={'reference': reference, 'price': price, 'quantity': quantity},
            extra_headers=extra_headers,
            extra_query=extra_query,
            extra_body=extra_body,
            timeout=timeout,
            max_retries=max_retries,
        )

